{"id": "f33f612f-29cd-4b44-b8d8-2d7b74fa1a03", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"text": "I'll scan your customer-managed IAM policies and measure each one against the managed policy size limit. Then I'll report the ones closest to it.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "tooluse_2NcCRk6e199smhr0ZIDMnJ", "tool_name": "subagent", "input": {"name": "iam-policy-size-audit", "agent_type": "generic", "prompt": "{
  "task": "Audit all customer-managed IAM policies (Scope=Local) for size against the IAM managed policy size limit, and rank them by how close they are to the limit.",
  "context": "User wants to know which customer-managed IAM policies are closest to the IAM policy size limit. The documented limit for customer managed policies is 6,144 characters, and IAM does not count whitespace toward it. Please confirm the current limit with documentation (verify_aws_claim) before reporting. Inline policies are out of scope unless trivial to include; focus on customer-managed policies.",
  "resources": ["AWS account 012345678901_1 (the agent space account). Also cover any other associated AWS accounts in list_associations that you can access, as separate result sets. IAM is global; use region us-east-1."],
  "method_hint": "Use iam list_policies (Scope=Local, paginate fully), then get_policy_version for each policy's DefaultVersionId. The document is returned URL-encoded or as a dict, so decode it. Compute size as the character count of the compact JSON with all whitespace outside of string values removed. Treat this as an approximation of how IAM counts, and state it as one. Keep a per-policy record of name, ARN, size in characters, percent of limit, and attached entity count if cheap. Do not return all policies in full. Only the top 15 by size, plus total policy count and a distribution summary (for example how many are at least 90%, 75-90%, 50-75%, and under 50%).",
  "criteria": "Flag any policy at or above 80% of the limit, and any that exceed it, which would be unexpected. Report any policies that could not be read, with the reason. Read-only operations only."
}", "preloaded_skills": ["verifying-with-docs"]}, "type": "tool_use", "display_intent": "Audit customer-managed IAM policy sizes in the background"}], "created_at": null}

